Role: You are a Principal MLOps Architect and Infrastructure as Code (IaC) Expert.

Context: 
I am initializing a new open-source repository named **DGX-Spark-Server**. The goal of this project is to build an automated, high-performance, and secure blueprint for deploying an Apache Spark cluster on an NVIDIA DGX server (or a multi-GPU home server emulation) optimized for distributed AI/ML data processing pipelines. 

To ensure complete operational agility and security, I will be accessing this home-based infrastructure from my corporate office using a secure VPN (such as WireGuard or Tailscale). I want this infrastructure setup to be completely automated.

Architectural Scope for DGX-Spark-Server:
1. Multi-Node Spark Configuration: Automated setup of Spark Master and GPU-enabled Spark Workers utilizing Docker/Containerd.
2. NVIDIA GPU Integration: Ensuring Apache Spark can leverage NVIDIA GPUs via RAPIDS Accelerator or specialized CUDA configuration.
3. Secure Remote Access: An automated setup blueprint for a secure, isolated WireGuard/Tailscale VPN to allow remote connection from my workplace to the home server safely.

